  children were secretly replaced with  these defective clones so that she could  have her pick of young easy  manipulatable spartan proteges on the  other side of the galaxy we have another  character who was similarly manipulated  and brainwashed at a young age this is  mckee who as a child saw the cruelty of  humanity when she was essentially a  slave laborer under unsc command it's  only when her planet was attacked by the  covenant an alien race hell-bent on  destroying humanity that it's discovered  she's a quote-unquote blessed one being  capable of activating ancient artifacts  that are critical in the covenant  religion she is brought under the  protection of mercy the eldest of three  leaders in the covenant high council  under his tutelage she learns of the  great journey a journey that will lead  the covenant to the sacred ring where  they will become gods of course the  great journey can't be completed without  a map and that's where these ancient  artifacts known as keystones come in  analysis of the keystone found on the  planet magical reveals them being over a  hundred thousand years old predating  humans and possibly even the covenant  it's likely that these keystones were  created by the forerunners an ancient  species worshiped by the covenant these  ring-like installations were created by  them as weapons against the flood a  parasitic alien race so both mckee and  master chief have some sort of ancestral  connection to the keystones the two of  them the only beings who can activate  its power even as a child john drew  pictures of the keystones this is how he  knew that two keystones needed to be  joined together to create the whole just  like how mckee and master chief will  literally join together while making  love the final episode is called  transcendence which makes sense  considering both the covenant and dr  halsey believe they can transcend their  respective species if they are able to  get a hold of this sacred ring dr halsey  believes that humanity is deeply flawed  and needs to transcend in order to save  it from itself  that's why they need us cortana  to save them from themselves it's almost  as if she wants to make humanity just  like her spartans devoid of emotion and  she's willing to go to great lengths to  do this even kidnapping and murdering  dozens of children as long as it's for  the good of mankind you kidnapped  mutilated and murdered dozens of  children to save billions more saving  humanity at the cost of your own master  chief is stuck between all these  competing parties the covenant who want  to destroy humanity the unsc who want to  control him and the spartans and dr  halsey who wants to use the ring for her  own twisted idea of how humanity should  evolve when master chief initially  touches the artifact it produces a ring  a ring which wreth calls a door to the  end of life both halsey and master chief  believe this to be a weapon one that can  be used to defeat the covenant mckee was  initially sent to the humans as a sort  of trojan horse tasked with infiltrating  the humans and retrieving the keystone  they acquired on madrigal but when she  meets jon the two form a connection and  for a brief moment she joins his side  this is symbolized when she removes the  covenant energy blade she had implanted  in her fingernail but this switching of  sides is short-lived when she is  brutally tased while in captivity which  conjures images from her past she has  these taser scars from when she was a  child an event which instilled in her  her hatred for humanity so she's able to  escape with the keystone and make it  back to the covenant the tragedy of  mckee however is that for all she's done  for the covenant they secretly want to  rid themselves of her  whether she realizes it or not she has  no home perhaps this is why she so  desperately wants to stay on that planet  with a sacred ring the unsc not only has  to deal with mckee escaping but also dr  hulsey you can tell they 