nes this is  why the high council is so pissed when  atriox kills master chief as this would  make finding the sacred ring now wholly  impossible and this event may be the  beginning of his separation from the  covenant in the games atriox leads a  group of covenant who join forces with  the unsc with the spartans on the  defensive and their time surely  outnumbered master chief is left with  only one option for cortana to fully  take control even though cortana says  she may not be able to bring him back he  says he trusts her which is ironic since  in episode 2 he said there is no one he  could trust except dr halsey who cortana  is modeled after master chief flatlines  in cortana takes over and because jon  isn't in control of master chief anymore  it allows cortana to pick up the ancient  keystone without it going all haywire  with their aircraft acting as a shield  the spartans are able to make their  escape the keystone intact and you'll  notice from the moment cortana takes  control master chief doesn't have any  dialogue and it will be interesting to  see if this continues into season two  chi as if jon is really himself but is  met with no response we don't know if  cortana will be able to give jon control  back and perhaps the only way that's  possible is if jon is reunited with  halsey then there's mckee whose body was  left back at the covenant temple i'm not  100 convinced she's gone for good after  all in a world where humans can be  cloned it's possible we may see her come  back especially since halsey had likely  done tests on her but the biggest  question mark in all this comes from a  character who we didn't even see in the  last episode quan ha a person whose  storyline seemed like it was its own  show altogether the big thread left  behind in her story is a portal that was  hinted at in episode 7. while on her  vision quest of sorts she is told that  she and her ancestors are integral in  accessing this well which is actually a  portal fueled by 